---
id: PY-010
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'named except handler whose body is only pass'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 5

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(except_clause) @target'

related: [PY-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A named `except` handler whose suite is only `pass` swallows the error on the
next line — the shape regex PY-004 cannot see. Catch the narrowest exception
you can handle and re-raise or log the rest. If swallowing really is correct,
suppress with that reason: `# @anvil-ignore PY-010 -- top-level guard, logs
and continues`.

Bare `except:` and inline `except Exception: pass` stay PY-004 (save-time
regex). This rule is the gate-time companion for the indented-`pass` form.
